{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q411535","formula":"C₁₆H₈O₂S₂","hill":"C16H8O2S2","elements":["H","C","O","S"],"composition":{"C":16.0,"H":8.0,"O":2.0,"S":2.0},"names":{"en":"Thioindigo","ru":"Тиоиндиго"},"descriptions":{"en":"Thioindigo is an organosulfur compound that is used to dye polyester fabric. A synthetic dye, thioindigo is related to the plant-derived dye indigo, replacing two NH groups with two sulfur atoms to create a shade of pink. Thioindigo is generated by the alkylation of the sulfur in thiosalicylic acid with chloroacetic acid.","ru":"Тиоинди́го (2,2′-бис-(3-оксобензо[b]тиенилиден), 2,2′-бис-тионафтениндиго) — органическое соединение с химической формулой C16H8O2S2O2. Имеет вид коричневых кристаллов, возгоняющихся с образованием паров оранжевого цвета. Получено немецким химиком Паулем Фридлендером в 1906 году."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":5378456,"mass":296.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C2C(=C1)C(=O)/C(=C\\3/C(=O)C4=CC=CC=C4S3)/S2","inchikey":"JOUDBUYBGJYFFP-FOCLMDBBSA-N","iupac":"(2E)-2-(3-oxo-1-benzothiophen-2-ylidene)-1-benzothiophen-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5378456","atoms":28,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.46,"y":1.626,"z":-0.001,"el":"S"},{"x":-1.46,"y":-1.626,"z":-0.001,"el":"S"},{"x":1.33,"y":-2.231,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.33,"y":2.231,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":0.661,"y":0.088,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.661,"y":-0.088,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":2.999,"y":-0.541,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.999,"y":0.54,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.056,"y":0.852,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.056,"y":-0.852,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.621,"y":-1.048,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.621,"y":1.048,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":4.145,"y":-1.323,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.145,"y":1.323,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":4.284,"y":1.497,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{